    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1414">

                <pb facs="0934" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/305.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to the confiscation of cotton by the Constitutionalists,
                    Department begs to inform you that it has this day received from Spanish
                    Ambassador advices to effect that Constitutionalists have not only refused to
                    permit Spaniards to redeem their cotton on payment of $15 per bale, but that
                    they have refused $20 from a great many Spaniards. Department hopes that you
                    will succeed in convincing Constitutionalist authorities of the inadvisability
                    and inexpediency of putting Spaniards in a class by themselves and demanding
                    from them more redemption than has been insisted upon from other foreigners. It
                    seems to this Department that the treatment of the Spaniards at Chihuahua and
                    Torreon has been very severe and that Constitutionalists should consider the
                    advisability of permitting Spaniards to redeem their cotton upon payment of same
                    amount as has been accepted from other foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
